      "Explanation": "The Buddha's birthday is the annual calendar observance of Shakyamuni's birth. In these records the headword chiefly appears as an editorial occasion label before a hall address or verse; one signed preface uses it to date a letter. The label establishes why the assembly met or a text was composed, but it is not itself part of the subsequent discourse and does not by itself mean the bathing rite performed on that day."
